    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q7a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the equation of the line $BC$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\frac12x+5$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{BC}&=\\frac{9-6}{8-2}\\\\m_{BC}&=\\frac12\\\\y-6&=\\frac12(x-2)\\\\y-6&=\\frac12x-1\\\\y&=\\frac12x+5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q7b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the equation of the line $AB$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=-x+8$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{AB}&=\\frac{6-4}{2-4}\\\\m_{AB}&=-1\\\\y-4&=-(x-4)\\\\y&=-x+8\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q7c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the equation of the line $AD$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=\\frac12x+2$\n\nOpposite sides are parallel, so $AD$ has the same gradient as $BC$.",
          "worked": "Since $AD\\parallel BC$, $m_{AD}=\\frac12$. Using $A(4,4)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-4&=\\frac12(x-4)\\\\y-4&=\\frac12x-2\\\\y&=\\frac12x+2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q7d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "the gradient of the line $CD$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-1$",
          "worked": "Since $CD\\parallel AB$, their gradients are equal. Thus $m_{CD}=m_{AB}=-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q7e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "the distance $AB$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt2$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}AB^2&=(2-4)^2+(6-4)^2\\\\AB^2&=4+4\\\\AB^2&=8\\\\AB&=2\\sqrt2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q7f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "the distance $CD$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2\\sqrt2$",
          "worked": "Opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal, so $CD=AB=2\\sqrt2$.",
